**Gaps:**
- `mulberry32`: seed `0` and negative seeds untested (bitwise ops on negative numbers in JS can behave unexpectedly).
- `sketchPath`: zero-point array (`[]`) not tested — only single-point is. A 3+ point multi-segment path is never exercised, so cross-segment jitter/step continuity is unverified.
- `barInsight`: no negative-value series, no all-zero series (division-by-zero guard beyond the "zero base" case), no `NaN`/`Infinity` guard.

```ts
describe("mulberry32 edge seeds", () => {
  it("handles seed 0 without throwing and stays in [0,1)", () => {
    const rnd = mulberry32(0);
    const v = rnd();
    expect(v).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(0);
    expect(v).toBeLessThan(1);
  });

  it("handles a negative seed deterministically", () => {
    const a = mulberry32(-5);
    const b = mulberry32(-5);
    expect(a()).toBe(b());
  });
});

describe("sketchPath edge cases", () => {
  it("returns an empty string for an empty points array", () => {
    expect(sketchPath([], mulberry32(1), 2)).toBe("");
  });

  it("builds a continuous path across 3+ points", () => {
    const d = sketchPath([[0,0],[10,0],[10,10]], mulberry32(1), 2, 7);
    expect(d.startsWith("M0.0 0.0")).toBe(true);
    expect(d.endsWith("L10.0 10.0")).toBe(true);
  });
});

describe("barInsight edge cases", () => {
  it("handles an all-negative series without NaN in the output", () => {
    const s = barInsight(d([-2, -5, -8]), fmt);
    expect(s).not.toContain("NaN");
  });

  it("handles a fully zero series (0 -> 0) without dividing by zero", () => {
    expect(barInsight(d([0, 0, 0]), fmt)).toContain("flat");
  });
});
```

