- **`incidentRealId`** only tests a single-colon id. A namespace value that itself contains a colon (e.g. an id embedding a URL or timestamp) isn't tested.
- **`incidentTone`**'s `?? "muted"` fallback for an out-of-map kind is dead-code-looking but untested — `KIND_TONE` is typed `Record<IncidentKind, IncidentTone>` so TS should make this unreachable, but a runtime value from an untyped source (DB row) could still hit it.

```ts
describe("incidentRealId multi-colon ids", () => {
  test("splits only on the first colon, keeping the rest of the id intact", () => {
    expect(incidentRealId("exec:a1b2:extra:00000000")).toBe("a1b2:extra:00000000");
  });
});

describe("incidentTone defensive fallback", () => {
  test("an incident kind absent from the map falls back to muted, never throws", () => {
    expect(incidentTone("unknown_kind" as never)).toBe("muted");
  });
});
```

